WEBVTT

0
00:00.200 --> 00:01.033
<v Krista>In this video,</v>

1
00:01.033 --> 00:02.270
we are talking about proportion,

2
00:02.270 --> 00:04.170
but in order to talk about proportion,

3
00:04.170 --> 00:07.340
we have to talk about ratios, so what is a ratio?

4
00:07.340 --> 00:09.360
Well, a ratio is just a fraction.

5
00:09.360 --> 00:10.610
Up until this point, we've gotten

6
00:10.610 --> 00:12.350
very comfortable talking about fractions,

7
00:12.350 --> 00:16.140
fractions just being 1/4, 2/3, 5/6,

8
00:16.140 --> 00:17.580
one number over another number,

9
00:17.580 --> 00:19.180
a numerator and a denominator.

10
00:19.180 --> 00:20.670
A ratio is exactly the same thing,

11
00:20.670 --> 00:22.870
it's a fraction, but we like to use a different word

12
00:22.870 --> 00:24.760
because we are really using ratio

13
00:24.760 --> 00:26.290
to describe something specific.

14
00:26.290 --> 00:27.920
We're talking about the ratio

15
00:27.920 --> 00:30.100
between one thing and another thing.

16
00:30.100 --> 00:32.490
In other words, if every time I go to the grocery store,

17
00:32.490 --> 00:34.750
I buy two apples and three oranges,

18
00:34.750 --> 00:36.390
and I always buy two apples

19
00:36.390 --> 00:38.210
and three oranges, if I double that,

20
00:38.210 --> 00:41.690
I'm going to buy four apples and six oranges, that's a ratio.

21
00:41.690 --> 00:44.070
In other words, my ratio is two to three.

22
00:44.070 --> 00:46.950
Every time I buy two apples, I buy three oranges.

23
00:46.950 --> 00:49.130
And no matter how many apples I buy,

24
00:49.130 --> 00:53.470
if I buy 10 apples, I multiplied my apple order by five,

25
00:53.470 --> 00:55.300
I'm going to have to multiply my orange order

26
00:55.300 --> 00:57.340
by five and buy 15 oranges.

27
00:57.340 --> 00:59.350
So I'd by 10 apples and 15 oranges.

28
00:59.350 --> 01:02.300
I always buy in that ratio, two to three.

29
01:02.300 --> 01:04.740
Now, a proportion is just two ratios

30
01:04.740 --> 01:07.170
or two fractions set equal to one another.

31
01:07.170 --> 01:09.010
So for example, in this problem,

32
01:09.010 --> 01:12.720
I have 20/36 equal to four over x.

33
01:12.720 --> 01:13.840
So I have two fractions

34
01:13.840 --> 01:16.160
or two ratios that are set equal to each other.

35
01:16.160 --> 01:18.230
So what I'm really asking here is,

36
01:18.230 --> 01:21.140
if 20 is to 36, four is to what,

37
01:21.140 --> 01:22.530
right, because I have this x here,

38
01:22.530 --> 01:23.990
I'm trying to solve for x.

39
01:23.990 --> 01:25.790
So I have this one fraction,

40
01:25.790 --> 01:27.510
this one ratio, that describes

41
01:27.510 --> 01:29.620
the relationship between two values.

42
01:29.620 --> 01:32.470
And I want to know what's the same relationship if

43
01:32.470 --> 01:34.610
instead of 20, I take four?

44
01:34.610 --> 01:36.780
When you're dealing with proportions like these ones,

45
01:36.780 --> 01:38.420
there's a couple things you want to remember.

46
01:38.420 --> 01:41.100
First, you want to see if you can reduce either fraction.

47
01:41.100 --> 01:42.930
We obviously can't reduce four over x,

48
01:42.930 --> 01:45.670
but we can reduce 20/36.

49
01:45.670 --> 01:48.230
We can divide both of these by four,

50
01:48.230 --> 01:51.778
so if we divide 20 by four, we're going to get five.

51
01:51.778 --> 01:53.698
If we divide 36 by four,

52
01:53.698 --> 01:56.448
we're going to get nine, so we get 5/9 equals four over x.

53
01:57.700 --> 01:59.360
We haven't changed this fraction at all,

54
01:59.360 --> 02:02.450
we just divided the numerator and the denominator by four,

55
02:02.450 --> 02:06.690
so we reduced it, and now we have 5/9 equals four over x.

56
02:06.690 --> 02:08.090
Now this equation says,

57
02:08.090 --> 02:09.520
if every times I give you five,

58
02:09.520 --> 02:10.990
you give me back nine, what

59
02:10.990 --> 02:13.170
are you going to give me back if I give you four?

60
02:13.170 --> 02:14.990
Now, in order to solve for x,

61
02:14.990 --> 02:16.040
and this is the other thing you need

62
02:16.040 --> 02:17.420
to remember with proportions,

63
02:17.420 --> 02:19.110
the easiest way to solve is just

64
02:19.110 --> 02:21.140
to do what we call cross multiplying,

65
02:21.140 --> 02:25.380
and all that means is that we're going to multiply five by x,

66
02:25.380 --> 02:27.600
and we're going to multiply nine by four.

67
02:27.600 --> 02:30.640
We just make a cross in the middle here and we multiply.

68
02:30.640 --> 02:34.610
So five times x is going to give me five x.

69
02:34.610 --> 02:39.240
Nine times four is going to give me 36, so I get 36.

70
02:39.240 --> 02:40.780
Now this is just a simple equation

71
02:40.780 --> 02:44.850
that I can solve for x by dividing both sides by five.

72
02:44.850 --> 02:46.780
When I divide both sides by five,

73
02:46.780 --> 02:49.610
I'll get five to cancel from the numerator and denominator,

74
02:49.610 --> 02:51.160
leaving me with just x on the left,

75
02:51.160 --> 02:55.110
so I get x is equal to 36/5.

76
02:55.110 --> 03:00.110
If I convert that to a mixed number, I can call this 7 1/5.

77
03:00.600 --> 03:03.500
So in other words, in order for these ratios to be equal,

78
03:03.500 --> 03:05.213
x has to be equal to 7 1/5.

79
03:06.740 --> 03:08.950
And so that just means if I give you 20

80
03:08.950 --> 03:10.710
and you give me 36 back,

81
03:10.710 --> 03:13.040
if the ratio holds, then when I give you four,

82
03:13.040 --> 03:15.160
you're going to give me 7 1/5 back

83
03:15.160 --> 03:17.260
in order for these things to be equal.

84
03:17.260 --> 03:18.790
So let's look at another example here.

85
03:18.790 --> 03:22.410
We have 2/4 is equal to x over 20, so again,

86
03:22.410 --> 03:24.420
we want to see if we can reduce either fraction,

87
03:24.420 --> 03:26.920
and in fact we can reduce the fraction on the left.

88
03:26.920 --> 03:28.410
We just need to divide the numerator

89
03:28.410 --> 03:30.200
and the denominator by two,

90
03:30.200 --> 03:33.590
and 2/4 reduces to the fraction 1/2.

91
03:33.590 --> 03:36.910
So we get 1/2 equals x over 20.

92
03:36.910 --> 03:38.670
With x in the numerator here,

93
03:38.670 --> 03:42.140
really all I'm saying is what's 1/2 of 20, right?

94
03:42.140 --> 03:45.670
Because if I just multiplied both sides by 20, I'd get 20

95
03:45.670 --> 03:48.180
to cancel on the right-hand side here in the denominator

96
03:48.180 --> 03:52.130
and I'd just be left with x is equal to 20 times 1/2,

97
03:52.130 --> 03:53.670
and of course I would get 10.

98
03:53.670 --> 03:54.740
We can see just by looking

99
03:54.740 --> 03:57.080
at this that x is going to be equal to 10,

100
03:57.080 --> 04:00.720
because if I say 1/2 equals x over 20, I know that x

101
04:00.720 --> 04:02.820
has to be 10 in order to make that true.

102
04:02.820 --> 04:04.640
In other words, I could look at it this way.

103
04:04.640 --> 04:09.450
I could say I have to multiply two by 10 to get 20,

104
04:09.450 --> 04:10.283
which means I'm going to have

105
04:10.283 --> 04:14.120
to multiply one by 10 to get whatever's over here,

106
04:14.120 --> 04:16.090
so I'd get 10 equals x.

107
04:16.090 --> 04:19.090
And again, this works if you just cross multiply.

108
04:19.090 --> 04:24.090
If we draw our x here and we say one times 20 gives us 20,

109
04:24.400 --> 04:27.590
and we say two times x gives us two x

110
04:27.590 --> 04:30.510
and then we divide both sides by two,

111
04:30.510 --> 04:33.930
20 over two gives us 10, so we'd get 10 equals x.

112
04:33.930 --> 04:34.990
So it works that way too,

113
04:34.990 --> 04:37.040
and cross multiplying will always work.

114
04:37.040 --> 04:39.150
You can use it every single time no matter what.

115
04:39.150 --> 04:40.780
So that's the easiest way to do it,

116
04:40.780 --> 04:43.260
but some of them will be simple enough you'll probably be

117
04:43.260 --> 04:45.950
able to get a guess for x just by looking at the problem,

118
04:45.950 --> 04:49.180
like this one where we said 1/2 was equal to x over 20.

119
04:49.180 --> 04:51.710
You can probably guess that x has to be 10,

120
04:51.710 --> 04:52.970
because these ratios,

121
04:52.970 --> 04:55.530
these fractions, have to be equal to each other,

122
04:55.530 --> 04:59.233
and you know that 1/2 is the same as 10 over x.